.TH "hatari-prg-profile" "1" "2026-10-18" "Hatari" "Hatari utilities"
.SH NAME
hatari\-prg\-profile \- profile performance of given Atari program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hatari\-prg\-profile
<\fIpath\fP> <\fIopcode\fP> [\fIoptions\fP]
.PP
.B hatari\-prg\-profile
<\fIreport\fP>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs given Atari program from GEMDOS HD with Hatari and profiles its
execution until program calls the specified GEMDOS \fIopcode\fP. Saves
the profile data, post-processes it, and shows overview of the
generated profile report.
.PP
If given existing profiling \fIreport\fP (not necessarily produced by
this utility), shows a summary of it.
.PP
Profiling requires program to have debug symbols; either included to
the binary itself, or in a separate "<program name>.sym" file.
.PP
Profile data is saved to same directory where the Atari program is,
and the report generated from it, is saved to the current directory.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B path
Path to Atari program to profile.
.TP
.B opcode
2-digit GEMDOS opcode in hex.
.TP
.B options
Extra options for provide for Hatari.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Profile program until it terminates with Pterm() (0x4C):
.B hatari\-prg\-profile ./hello.tos 4C
.TP
Profile OPL2 DSP midiplayer until Fcreate() (0x3C), under Falcon emulation:
.B hatari\-prg\-profile ./f030mid.tos 3C \-\-machine falcon \-s 4
.SH FILES
After succesful profiling run, current directory includes following
files:
.TP
.I profile-data.txt
Profile disassembly and symbol callgraph information, saved at the end
of the profiling.  Disassembly is annotated with per-address counts of
how many times given instruction was run and how many cycles that
used.
.IP
For machines with emulated cache, address annotations include also
number of instruction cache misses and data cache hits.
.TP
.I profile-report.txt
Profiling report generated by post-processing the
\fIprofile-data.txt\fP file. Shows how long the profile run took
(which can be used for timing program performance), and sorted lists
of which program symbols were called most often, how many cycles
(time) code under those took etc.
.SH NOTES
While whole program profiling can be useful by itself (depending on
program), this script can also be used e.g. as a starting point for
automating profiling of more specific parts of the program. That would
require (at least) setting up suitable (program-specific) breakpoints
(to start profiling and save the data) for relevant points in its
execution.
.PP
Script does not generate callgraphs because for more complex programs
finding suitable post-processing options for reducing callgraph to a
readable size, while still retaining relevant information, can take
quite a lot of iteration.
.PP
In simple programs though, only thing needed for reasonable
callgraphs, is re-running the post-processor command (shown by the
script) with an additional "\-g" option, and viewing the resulting
\fIGraphviz\fP ".dot" files with (e.g.) \fIxdot\fP utility.
.PP
For more info, see: https://www.hatari\-emu.org/doc/debugger.html#Profiling
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR hatari (1), xdot (1)
